From ff857ee63a142bec3d48e08436bb736abcfb2aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 01:09:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): harden 0.1.0 first-run (jq soft-fail, kernel
 brand, init nudge, AGENTS.md backup)

Focused setup-hardening for a clean-box first run:

1. jq is no longer a fatal prerequisite. checkPrerequisites downgrades a
   missing jq from an error to a warning so `npx forge setup` completes on a
   clean box (esp. Windows); workflow helper scripts that need jq degrade or
   defer. checkPrerequisites now returns a structured { errors, warnings, ok }
   so embedding agents can inspect state instead of only observing a process
   exit. Genuinely-fatal prereqs (git, node, required gh) still hard-exit.
   (kernel 01468e44)

2. Kernel-brand the issue-store surfaces. Setup STEP 2 now reads
   "Issue tracking (Forge Kernel) - zero-install, git-backed" to match the
   Issue Store prompt, and the standard adoption profile's generated
   .forge/config.yaml sets adapters.issue.primary to kernel. (kernel 5021a1f8)

3. Complete first-run. Plain interactive, --agents, quick, and legacy
   interactive setup never wrote .forge/config.yaml; they now print a
   prominent "NEXT: run `forge init`" step (skipped when config already
   exists). (kernel 5bdc91d3, partial)

4. Guard markerless AGENTS.md. The non-interactive quick path overwrote an
   existing markerless (pre-Forge) AGENTS.md unconditionally; it now snapshots
   the file to AGENTS.md.bak and warns before overwrite. (kernel a5399f3d)

Tests: new test/setup-hardening.test.js covers the jq soft-fail contract,
kernel primary in adoption profiles, the init next-step nudge, and the
AGENTS.md backup guard; setup-runtime-flags jq test updated to the new
non-fatal contract.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
